Algorithm 2: [s,a,C, h,y]=forward(x,wh,wx,b,wy,by) % forward propagation of SWLSTM
input:
x: features of a batch of training set or test set
[wh,wx,b]: weight and bias [wy, by]:  weight and bias
output:
s: shared gates of all samples in x a: information state of all samples in x
C:  cell state of all samples in x h: output of hidden layer of all samples in x
y: output of output layer of all samples in x
1: for t = 1:length(x)
2: net(t) = wh·h(t-1) + wx·x(t) + b;
3: s(t) = σ(net(t));
4: a(t) = tanh(net(t));
5: C(t) = s(t)*C(t-1) + (1-s(t))*a(t);
6: h(t) = s(t)*tanh(C(t));
7: z(t) = wy·h(t) + by
8: y(t) = σ(z(t));
9: end
Algorithm 3: [δWh,δWx,δB,δWy,δBy]=back(x,Y,s,a,C, h,y) % back propagation of SWLSTM
input:
x: features of a batch of training set or test set
Y: labels corresponding to x
s, a, C, h, y: forward propagation results corresponding to x
output:
δWh: average gradient of Wh in batch [x,Y] δWx: average gradient of Wx in batch [x,Y]
δB:  average gradient of B in batch [x,Y] δWy: average gradient of Wy in batch [x,Y]
δBy: average gradient of By in batch [x,Y]
1: for t = length(x):t
2: δy(t) = y(t) - Y(t);
3: δz(t) = δy(t) * [y(t)*(1-y(t))];
4: δwy = δz(t)·h(t);
5: δby = δz(t);
6: if t == length(x)
7: δh(t) = δz(t) wy;
8: δC(t) = δh(t)*s(t)*[1-tanh2(C(t))];
9: else:
10: δh(t) = δz(t) wy + δnet(t+1) wh;
11: δC(t) = δh(t)*s(t)*[1-tanh2(C(t))]+ δC(t+1)*s(t);
12: end
13: δa(t) = δC(t)*(1-s(t));
14: δs(t) = δh(t)*tanh(C(t)) + δC(t)*[C(t-1)-a(t)];
15: δnet(t) = δa(t)*[1-a(t)2]+ δs(t)*[s(t)*(1-s(t))];
16: δwh = δnet(t) h(t-1);
17: δwx = δnet(t) x(t);
18: δb = δnet(t);
19: δWy+=δwy; δBy+=δby; δWh+=δwh; δWx+=δwx; δB+=δb;
20: end
21: δWy/= length(x); δBy/= length(x); δWh/= length(x); δWx/= length(x); δB/= length(x);
Z. Zhang, et al. Applied Energy 247 (2019) 270–284
